    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22205" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γίγγρ-ας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>small Phoenician flute</i> or <i>fife</i>, of a high
			pitch and plaintive tone, <i><span class="en">
				Amphis
				14
			</span></i> (from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γίγγρης</span>, Phoenician
			name for Adonis, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				4.174f
			</span></i>):—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γίγγρος</span></b> 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					108
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				259
			</span></i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γίγγρον</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>its music</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Trypho
				<u>Fr.</u>
				109
			</span></i> V.; <i>dance to its tune</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.102
			</span></i>.</div>
